FreeSDN backend
===============

The backend provides the FastAPI API, PostgreSQL data model and migrations,
Celery workers, and managed-device adapters for FreeSDN Community Edition /
Early Access. It is one component of the appliance, not a standalone supported
deployment or an independently qualified PyPI distribution.

Use the repository's root README, install.sh and docker/RELEASE-SUPPORT for
installation and supported deployment boundaries. The qualified appliance
build uses the committed Poetry lockfile and the shipped Docker recipes.
Do not substitute a bare uvicorn process for the complete deployment.

Development
-----------
Create an isolated environment with the Python and Poetry versions used by the
Dockerfile and CI. From this directory, validate metadata with:

    poetry check --lock

Install development dependencies with:

    poetry install --no-root

Configure disposable database and broker services before running integration
tests or migrations. The application migration entry point is:

    poetry run python scripts/migrate.py

Use ADAPTER_READ_ONLY=true and synthetic/disposable device targets for tests.
Keep credentials out of source control. Preserve the vault encryption keys
separately from data backups; authentication recovery may require a separate
JWT signing-key change. Follow docker/TOKEN-REVOCATION-UPGRADING in the parent
directory for the qualified recovery boundary.

Release status
--------------
A version string, metadata check or wheel build is not evidence that a public
release, upgrade, hardware workflow, backup restore or enterprise service level
has passed acceptance. Refer to the exact candidate commit and its qualification
record. The backend's runtime version comes from app/__init__.py; pyproject.toml
and the frontend metadata mirror it.

